  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe first step of [close a top-level traversable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#close-a-top-level-traversable) states:\r\n\r\n> 1. If traversable's is closing is true, then return.\r\n\r\nHowever, the only formal caller of this operation is [`window.close`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#dom-window-close), which has the following steps:\r\n\r\n> 1. Set thisTraversable's is closing to true.\r\n> 2. Queue a task on the DOM manipulation task source to close thisTraversable.\r\n\r\nSo the `is closing` flag is always true when we reach the first step to close the top-level traversable.",
